# Copy this file to tools/emulator.env and edit it for your machine.
#
#   cp tools/emulator.env.example tools/emulator.env
#
# tools/emulator.env is gitignored; this example is committed so a fresh clone knows which
# knobs exist. Anything already exported in your shell beats the file, so you can override one
# value for a single run without editing anything:
#
#   AVD_NAME=other_avd tools/emulator.sh up
#
# Every value below is OPTIONAL - the script works out sane defaults on its own, and only names
# no one's home directory. Set what actually differs on your machine.

# Android SDK root. Leave unset if ANDROID_HOME, ANDROID_SDK_ROOT or the platform default
# (%LOCALAPPDATA%\Android\Sdk on Windows, ~/Library/Android/sdk on macOS) is right.
# ANDROID_HOME=C:/Users/you/AppData/Local/Android/Sdk

# Needed only by sdkmanager/avdmanager, which are .bat/.sh launchers that read JAVA_HOME directly
# rather than looking along PATH. Leave unset if `java` on PATH points into a JDK - the script
# derives it - or if cmdline-tools is already installed and no SDK package needs installing.
# JAVA_HOME=C:/Users/you/scoop/apps/temurin21-jdk/current

# Emulator/AVD tuning. Defaults are in tools/emulator.sh.
# AVD_NAME=bookreader_test
# SYS_IMAGE is quoted because the file is sourced by bash: without quotes the semicolons end the
# assignment and the rest is run as commands.
# SYS_IMAGE="system-images;android-36;google_apis_playstore;x86_64"
# DEVICE_PROFILE=pixel_6
# PKG=com.fpedroso.bookreader

# Point at a different env file for a single run (default: tools/emulator.env).
# EMULATOR_ENV=/path/to/other.env
